1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,990
Hey! I'm all packed and ready to go.
嘿，我都打包好可以走了

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:10,330
That's right. Daddy and Uncle Joey are going on a trip today.
沒錯，爹地跟喬伊叔叔今天要出門去

3
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:15,140
We're going to a conference in Barbados. Right? Can you say, "Barbados"?
我們要去參加一個在巴貝多的研討會 你會說「巴貝多」嗎？

4
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:17,280
Barbados.
巴貝多

5
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:23,270
Okay. I've gotta say, it means so much to me that you guys are coming..
我覺得要你們 到那麼遠的地方去…

6
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:26,150
all the way over there to hear me give my speech.
聽我的演講，對我真是意義重大

7
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:29,260
And I have a surprise. I had to pull some strings..
我讓要你們高興一下 我費盡功夫…

8
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:34,450
but I was able to get everyone passes to the entire conference. That's right!
幫大家爭取到整個研討會的通行證 沒錯！

9
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:41,100
These babies will get you into all the paleontology lectures and seminars.
這些寶貝可以讓你們自由參加所有的 古生物學演講或是研討會

10
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:45,370
Do you have anything that will get us out of them?
你有什麼東西 是可以讓我們不用參加的嗎？

11
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:49,310
We're excited to hear the speech, but the rest of the time..
我們真的很興奮要聽你的演講 但是其他的時間…

12
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,380
we're gonna want to do island stuff.
我們想要做一些島上活動

13
00:00:51,610 --> 00:00:53,810
David will probably want to hear a few lectures.
大衛或許會想要聽幾場演說

14
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:56,010
- Right, because he's a scientist. - No, no.
-沒錯，因為他是科學家 -不，不

15
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:59,950
He's been in Minsk for eight years. If he gets too much direct sunlight..
他在明斯克待了八年 如果他在陽光下太久…

16
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:01,820
he'll die.
他會死的

17
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:03,890
- Okay, we'd better go. - Yeah?
-好的，我們最好出發了 -是嗎？

18
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,890
- So we'll see you guys tomorrow. - All right, let's do it.
-那我們明天見 -好的，明天見

19
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:09,790
A five-hour flight with Charlie, have a couple drinks..
跟查莉一起飛行五個小時，喝幾杯酒…

20
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,460
get under that blanket and do what comes natural.
在毛毯下做一些自然會發生的事

21
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:15,860
It's a blanket, Joe, not a cloak of invisibility.
那是毛毯，喬伊，不是隱形大衣

22
00:01:17,677 --> 00:01:19,668
The One In Barbados

00:01:20,677 --> 00:01:21,668
rainystar壓制iPod-MP4

23
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:18,150
- Wow, this place is beautiful! - Look at all these paleontologists!
-哇，這地方真漂亮！ -瞧瞧這些古生物學家！

24
00:02:18,330 --> 00:02:22,600
I know. There are gonna be some pasty folks by the pool tomorrow.
我知道 明天游泳池旁一定有許多蒼白的人

25
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:27,040
- My God, I can't believe you're here! - I think I've been recognized.
-我的天啊，我不敢相信你在這裡！ -我想我被認出來了

26
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:31,410
- This happens all the time. - Dr. Geller? I am such a huge fan.
-這常常發生的 -蓋勒博士？我真是仰慕你

27
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:34,080
That never happens.
這倒是從來沒有發生過

28
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:38,690
I've been following your career for years. I can't wait for your keynote speech.
我多年以來一直很注意你的研究 我等不及要聽你的演說了

29
00:02:38,890 --> 00:02:43,260
- Wow! This is very flattering. - I would love your autograph.
-哇，你太過獎了 -我會很想要你的簽名的

30
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:45,590
Well, sure.
喔，當然

31
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:48,590
- "Dear..?" - Sarah.
-親愛的？ -莎拉

32
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:54,070
"Sarah. I dig you."
「莎拉，我挖（喜歡）你」

33
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:58,470
- "Dr. Ross Geller." - Oh, thank you so much.
-「羅斯蓋勒博士上」 -哇，真是太謝謝你了

34
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:02,910
Sure. Sarah, I'd like you to introduce you to my colleague, Professor Wheeler.
不客氣，莎拉，讓我幫你介紹一下 我同事，魏勒教授

35
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:07,070
- And this is Joey Tribbiani. - Are you a paleontologist?
-這位是喬伊崔比亞尼 -你是古生物學家嗎？

36
00:03:07,450 --> 00:03:10,710
No, God, no, no. I'm an actor.
不，天啊，不，我是演員

37
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:14,720
You probably recognize me from a little show called The Days of Our Lives.
你或許有看過我演的一出小戲叫做 《那個我們的日子》

39
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:19,950
Dude, it's just Days of Our Lives. There's no "the."
老兄，只是《我們的日子》 沒有「那個」

41
00:03:23,230 --> 00:03:29,430
Okay, Ross. Boy, you.. Yeah. No, no. I play Dr. Drake Ramoray.
好的，羅斯，天啊，你…是啊 不，我扮演德克羅曼瑞醫生

42
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:35,340
- I'm sorry. I don't own a TV. - You don't own a TV?
-我很抱歉，我家沒有電視 -你家沒有電視？

43
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:38,140
What's all your furniture pointed at?
那你家的家俱是擺向哪個方向呢？

44
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:45,310
- Well, it was a pleasure to meet you all. - You too, Sarah.
-很榮幸認識你們 -我們也是，莎拉，再見

45
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,690
Jeez, who doesn't own a TV?
天啊，這年頭誰沒有電視呢？

46
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:50,260
Well, actually, I don't.
嗯，事實上，我沒有

47
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:53,330
Yeah, and mine broke two months ago and I still haven't gotten a new one.
是啊，我的兩個月前壞了 還沒買新的

48
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:56,190
Well, didn't you two come to the right convention.
那你們兩個還真是來對研討會了

49
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:00,830
David, can you help me?
大衛，你可以幫個忙嗎？

50
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,670
I'm trying to explain to Chandler how a plane stays in the air.
我正在跟錢德解釋 飛機是怎麼漂浮在空中的

51
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,570
Certainly. That's a combination of Bernoulli's Principle..
當然，那是波諾利原理加上…

52
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:11,270
- and Newton's third law of motion. - See?
-牛頓第三運動定律 -知道了嗎？

53
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:14,900
Yeah. That's the same as, "It has something to do with wind."
是啊，那還真是跟 「跟風有關的」一樣

54
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:17,920
I'm gonna go pick up a few things for the trip.
我要去為這次旅行買幾樣東西

55
00:04:18,090 --> 00:04:22,680
I should go too. Now, tomorrow do you want to share a cab to the airport..
我也應該走了 明天你們要一起搭計程車到機場嗎？

56
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,650
or should Mike and I meet you?
還是說我跟麥克到機場跟你們碰面呢？

57
00:04:29,030 --> 00:04:32,400
Mike? Who's Mike?
麥克？誰是麥克呢？

58
00:04:33,030 --> 00:04:36,230
- Mike's your ex-boyfriend. - That's right!
-麥克是你的前男友 -沒錯！

59
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:40,100
Oh, yeah. Wow, I had totally forgotten about him.
哇，我已經完全忘了他了

60
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:46,210
- That's a blast from the past, huh? - No, it's okay. Honest mistake.
-難忘往日情懷脫口而出嗎？ -不，沒關係的，無心之過

61
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:49,110
It really doesn't mean anything. I mean, you know..
那真的不代表什麼 我是說，你知道的…

62
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:52,280
Monica refers to Chandler as Richard all the time.
摩妮卡也常常把錢德叫成李察

63
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:58,220
- She does? - Let's get you out of here.
-她有嗎？ -我們快讓你離開吧

64
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:06,330
Well, at least you took me down with you.
至少你也拖我下水了

65
00:05:06,570 --> 00:05:10,000
I'm so sorry. I just.. I keep thinking about Mike.
我很抱歉，我只是… 我一直在想麥克

66
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:14,070
I'm crazy about David, and we're having so much fun together.
我非常喜歡大衛 而且我們在一起很開心

67
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:18,240
Why? Why do I miss Mike? That's just.. That's gonna go away, right?
為什麼我會想念麥克？這真是… 這會消逝的，對嗎？

68
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:20,440
- Well, I guess. In time. - Yeah.
-嗯，我猜是吧，總有一天 -是啊

69
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:23,550
I mean, my feelings for Richard are certainly gone.
我是說我對李察的感覺 都已經消失了

70
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:29,310
You just did it again. Chandler. Your feelings for Chandler are certainly gone.
你又來了，是錢德 你對錢德的感覺都已經消失了

71
00:05:32,190 --> 00:05:34,960
Boy, Phoebe's still pretty hung up on that Mike, huh?
天啊，菲比還在想麥克嗎？

72
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:38,160
I wouldn't read too much into it.
我不會想太多的

73
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:41,530
Still, a girl calls you by her ex-boyfriend's name..
但是女生把你叫成 她前男友的名字…

74
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:44,760
- that's not a good thing, right? - Let me stop you there.
-那不是什麼好事，不是嗎？ -讓我先打斷你一下

75
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:49,600
Because I think I see where this is going. I'm not very good at giving advice.
因為我想我知道這是怎麼回事了 我對給人建議不太行

76
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:52,610
See, if you want advice, go to Ross or Monica. Or Joey..
如果你想知道披薩的餡料或是 為何尿尿時有灼熱感之類的…

77
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:58,180
for advice about pizza toppings or a burning sensation when you pee.
建議，那就去找羅斯或是 摩妮卡或是喬伊

78
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:03,590
I'm sorry, I just wish there was something I could do, you know?
很抱歉，我只是希望能做點什麼 你知道嗎？

79
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:07,460
- Well, you know Phoebe.. - Seriously, we're gonna do this?
-嗯，你知道菲比… -真的，我們要這樣嗎？

80
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:11,290
I'm sorry, I just wish I could make her forget about Mike already.
很抱歉，我只希望我能讓她忘了麥克

81
00:06:11,570 --> 00:06:16,300
- Why did Phoebe and Mike break up? - Because his penis was too big.
-菲比跟麥克為什麼分手呢？ -因為他的老二太大了

82
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:23,600
I'm sorry. That's the kind of thing I do.
抱歉，那才是我擅長的事

83
00:06:24,610 --> 00:06:27,670
They broke up because Mike didn't want to get married.
他們分手是因為麥克不想要結婚

84
00:06:27,850 --> 00:06:30,480
What if you let Phoebe know you'd be open to marriage?
如果讓菲比知道 你對婚姻沒有異議呢？

85
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:34,920
That's great. That's great. I'll propose to her.
太棒了，太棒了，我會跟她求婚

86
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:37,460
What?
什麼？

87
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:39,990
I was probably going to do it at some point.
反正我遲早都會這麼做的

88
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:43,230
- No, I didn't mean now. - Well, why not? It's brilliant.
-不，我沒有說現在 -為何不呢？這實在太聰明了

89
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:46,230
"Goodbye, Mike. We'll see you at the wedding, fella.
再見，麥克，我們婚禮見，老兄

90
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:49,300
Well, we probably won't invite you to the wedding, but.."
我們可能也不會 邀請你參加婚禮，但是…

91
00:06:49,470 --> 00:06:53,000
- Well, thank you, Chandler. Sincerely. - Well, you're welcome.
-衷心地謝謝你，錢德 -不用客氣

92
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:55,140
Glad I could help.
很高興能夠幫得上忙

93
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:59,880
- How do you think I should propose? - I'm pretending to read here.
-你認為我該怎麼求婚呢？ -我在假裝閱讀

94
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,710
I'm sorry.
抱歉

95
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:07,950
Yeah. How you doing? Hey, how are you?
你好嗎？嘿，你好嗎？

96
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:13,190
You said you were gonna wear a thong. Where's the thong?
你說你要穿丁字褲的，丁字褲呢？

97
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:18,730
I didn't mean a thong. I meant thongs.
我不是說丁字褲 我是說夾腳涼鞋

98
00:07:20,230 --> 00:07:22,900
You really should have been more clear about that.
你應該要說清楚的

99
00:07:28,610 --> 00:07:31,410
You're never gonna guess who I just saw downstairs.
你們不會相信我在樓下看到誰

100
00:07:32,110 --> 00:07:33,840
Britney Spears!
小甜甜布蘭妮！

101
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:37,250
Yeah. She never misses these conferences.
是啊，她從來不會錯過 這些研討會的

102
00:07:37,550 --> 00:07:41,010
- No, I just saw Dr. Kenneth Schwartz! - Oh, my God!
-我剛剛看到肯尼斯史華茲博士！ -喔，我的天啊！

103
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:42,710
- I know! - Did you talk to him?
-我知道 -你有跟他說話嗎？

104
00:07:42,890 --> 00:07:46,190
Oh, yeah. What am I gonna say to Kenneth Schwartz?
是喔，我要跟 肯尼斯史華茲說什麼呢？

105
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:50,460
You could say, "Hey, Kenny, how come you're not Britney Spears?"
你可以說「嗨，肯尼 為什麼你不是小甜甜布蘭妮呢？」

106
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:53,530
- You ready to go? - You're gonna go now?
-你準備好要走了嗎？ -你現在就要走了嗎？

107
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:57,540
- I thought we could hang out. - I can't. I have seminars all day.
-我以為我們可以在一起度過 -我不行，我整天都有研討會

108
00:07:57,710 --> 00:07:59,830
I promised Ross I'd look at his speech.
我答應羅斯我會看看他的演說稿

109
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:06,110
But maybe we could have dinner later? Out on the balcony? It'll be romantic.
但是或許我們晚點可以共進晚餐 在陽台外面，會很浪漫的

110
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:08,470
Will you wear a thong?
你可以穿丁字褲嗎？

111
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,410
I will if you will.
你穿我就穿

112
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:14,420
You got yourself a very weird deal.
你的交換條件真是奇怪

113
00:08:16,890 --> 00:08:19,420
I'm good. I have dinner plans.
我很好，我晚餐已經有安排了

114
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,920
- So you gonna be okay? - Yeah, yeah.
-你一個人可以嗎？ -是的，可以

115
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:27,160
I got tons of stuff I could do. I'm gonna hit the beach, go swimming.
我有很多事可以做 我要去海灘，去游泳

116
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:29,130
Joe, have you looked outside?
喬伊，你有看看外面嗎？

117
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,730
No. Why?
沒有，為什麼呢？

118
00:08:34,410 --> 00:08:37,170
- Oh, man. - There's an indoor pool.
-天啊 -這裡有室內游泳池

119
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:38,570
- You could swim there. - Yeah.
-你可以在那邊游泳 -是啊

120
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:42,270
I wasn't gonna swim. I was gonna dig a hole.
我沒有要游泳，我是要去挖洞的

121
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:49,810
That Mike thing was interesting. I don't know what's gonna happen..
麥克那件事真是有趣，我不知道…

122
00:08:49,990 --> 00:08:54,620
- with Phoebe and David. - I do. Want a hint, huh?
-菲比跟大衛之間會發生什麼事 -我知道，想要個提示嗎？

123
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,400
I do.
我願意

124
00:08:58,230 --> 00:09:00,130
I do.
我願意

125
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:04,370
Okay, I'm sensing this is some kind of wordplay..
好的，我可以感到 這是什麼文字遊戲的

126
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:07,630
because you are pink with barely controlled glee.
因為你已經有點 無法控制的興奮發紅了

127
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:12,840
- David's gonna propose to Phoebe. - What? Why?
-大衛要跟菲比求婚了 -什麼？為什麼？

128
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:16,380
Because we were talking about ways he could beat Mike..
因為我們本來在談 有哪些他可以贏過麥克的方式

129
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:18,850
and I told him Phoebe wanted to get married.
而我告訴他菲比想要結婚

130
00:09:19,190 --> 00:09:21,120
Chandler, we have talked about this.
錢德，我們已經談過了

131
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:24,280
You are not supposed to give people advice!
你不可以給別人建議的！

132
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:28,790
Couldn't you have made some inappropriate joke?
你不能說一些什麼 不適宜的笑話就好了嗎？

133
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,430
I did!
我說了！

134
00:09:31,930 --> 00:09:33,590
A penis one!
一個老二的笑話！

135
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,700
Just so I know, what was so wrong about what I said?
說明一下，我說的有什麼不對的呢？

136
00:09:36,870 --> 00:09:38,930
They've only been going out for a few weeks.
他們才交往幾個星期而已

137
00:09:39,170 --> 00:09:43,580
Phoebe is completely hung up on Mike. I mean, she'll say no..
菲比還無法忘記麥克 我想她會拒絕的

138
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:47,240
David's heart will be broken, it'll be too hard for them to recover..
然後大衛的心會碎 他們會很難復合

139
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:50,350
and then Phoebe will end up alone again.
而然後菲比又會是孤單的一個人

140
00:09:50,850 --> 00:09:53,340
Man, that's some bad advice.
天啊，真是糟糕的建議

141
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:03,360
Oh, hey. Thank God. You guys are here.
感謝上帝你們來了

142
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:06,760
- What's going on? - Everything is upside-down here.
-怎麼了？ -這裡的一切都不對勁

143
00:10:06,930 --> 00:10:12,870
It rains all day long and nobody watches TV, and Ross is famous.
整天都在下雨，沒有人看電視 而且羅斯還很有名氣

144
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:16,740
I don't want to alarm anybody..
我不想要驚動大家…

145
00:10:16,910 --> 00:10:20,440
but Monica's hair is twice as big as it was when we landed.
但是摩妮卡的頭髮 比下飛機時大了一倍

146
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:23,320
Okay. When I go places with high humidity..
好了，當我去高濕度地區的時候…

147
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:26,920
it gets a little extra body, okay?
頭髮就會比較蓬鬆，好嗎？

148
00:10:27,090 --> 00:10:31,290
That's why our honeymoon photos look like me and Diana Ross.
那就是為什麼我們的蜜月照 看起來是我跟戴安娜羅絲

149
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,260
I'll show you guys where to check in.
我帶你們去登記住房

150
00:10:33,430 --> 00:10:36,660
Oh, honey? Can you make sure we get a king-size bed?
親愛的，你可以確定我們可以拿到 超大尺寸的床嗎？

151
00:10:36,830 --> 00:10:41,390
Oh, David, get one for us too. Oh, and see if they have a heart-shaped one.
大衛，也幫我們確定一下 還有看看他們有沒有心型的床

152
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:44,590
And with mirrors on the ceiling.
而有天花板上要有鏡子

153
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:48,500
And make sure our room isn't next to theirs.
還有確定我們的房間 不要在他們的隔壁

154
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:51,940
Oh, you guys are so lucky you're here with people.
喔，你們真幸運 有人陪你們到這裡

155
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:53,910
I'd love to share this with someone.
我真想跟某人分享這一切

156
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:57,570
Oh, honey, you have us. We love you.
親愛的，你有我們，我們愛你

157
00:10:57,750 --> 00:11:01,920
Okay, which one of you is gonna sleep with me?
太好了，你們誰要跟我睡？

158
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,680
You know, it's just such a romantic place.
這是個很浪漫的地方

159
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:09,630
I just wish I could share it with a guy.
我只希望可以跟一個男人共度

160
00:11:11,130 --> 00:11:13,230
- Not Joey. - Not Joey. No.
-不是喬伊 -不是喬伊，不是

161
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:18,500
- I was just lusting after Chandler. - Yeah, right.
-我只是在垂涎錢德 -是啊，沒錯

162
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:25,580
So.. I'm proposing to Phoebe tonight.
我今晚要跟菲比求婚了

163
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:27,280
Tonight?
今晚？

164
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:31,070
Isn't an engagement ring supposed to have a diamond?
訂婚戒指不是應該要有鑽石的嗎？

165
00:11:31,890 --> 00:11:34,410
Oh, there it is.
喔，在這裡

166
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:38,920
Yes, well, being a failed scientist doesn't pay quite as well as you might think.
是啊，一個失敗的科學家 並沒有你想的賺的多

167
00:11:39,330 --> 00:11:42,350
That's one-seventieth of a carat.
那是七十分之一克拉

168
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,430
And the clarity is quite poor.
清晰度是很差

169
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:50,060
Nice.
很好

170
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:54,600
- Monica, can I talk to you for a second? - Okay.
-摩妮卡，我可以跟你談一下嗎？ -好的

171
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,610
David's gonna propose to Phoebe tonight.
大衛要在今晚跟菲比求婚

172
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:59,750
See what happens when you give people advice?
瞧瞧這就是你給別人建議的後果

173
00:12:00,410 --> 00:12:03,540
- Well, I hope you told him not to. - That would be advice!
-我希望你有告訴他不可以 -那又會是一個建議了！

174
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:07,650
Okay, fine. I'll handle this.
好的，沒關係，讓我來處理

175
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:12,220
- Phoebe? - Yeah?
-菲比？ -怎樣？

176
00:12:12,730 --> 00:12:16,890
- I need to talk to you. - Are you leaving the Supremes?
-我需要跟你談談 -你要離開你的主宰了嗎？

177
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:28,530
Okay, my husband just gave your boyfriend some very bad advice.
我老公剛給了你男友 一個很糟糕的建議

178
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:30,900
David's gonna propose to you tonight.
大衛今晚要跟你求婚了

179
00:12:31,510 --> 00:12:33,570
Wow, really?
哇，真的嗎？

180
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:37,610
That's fantastic!
這實在太棒了！

181
00:12:38,490 --> 00:12:41,350
What? Are you serious? You want to marry him?
什麼？你是說真的嗎？你想嫁給他？

182
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:44,510
- What about Mike? - Oh, okay, you want me to marry Mike?
-那麥克呢？ -好的，你要我嫁給麥克是嗎？

183
00:12:44,730 --> 00:12:46,920
Let's just gag him and handcuff him..
讓我們把他塞住嘴巴 用手銬銬住他

184
00:12:47,090 --> 00:12:49,430
and force him down the aisle, okay?
然後逼他踏上紅毯，好嗎？

185
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:52,290
I can just see it. "Mike, do you take Phoebe?"
我已經可以預見到 「麥克，你願意娶菲比嗎？」

186
00:12:54,970 --> 00:12:58,460
You know? It's every girl's dream.
你知道嗎？真是每個女孩的夢想

187
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:02,130
Do you really think marrying someone else is the right answer?
你真的認為嫁給別人是對的？

188
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:06,610
Sure. Look, okay, bottom line? I love Mike.. David!
當然，聽著，最重要的是 我愛麥克…大衛！

189
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:10,380
David! I love David.
大衛！我愛大衛！

190
00:13:10,550 --> 00:13:13,540
Don't look at me that way, Roseanne Roseannadanna.
別那樣看我，戴安娜羅絲

191
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:22,460
"By using CT scans and computer imaging, we can, in a very real way..
借由使用中央標準掃瞄法跟電腦影像 我們可以以非常真實的方式…

192
00:13:22,630 --> 00:13:27,260
bring the Mesozoic Era into the 21st century."
將中生代時期帶進二十一世紀

193
00:13:29,170 --> 00:13:30,660
It's great.
太棒了

194
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,640
Yeah, you really think so?
你真的這麼認為嗎？

195
00:13:32,810 --> 00:13:34,600
You'll be the hit of the conference.
你將成為此次研討會的焦點

196
00:13:34,810 --> 00:13:36,370
It'll be even better tomorrow..
明天還會更好

197
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:39,170
because I won't be constantly interrupted by Joey..
因為我不會一直被喬伊打斷…

198
00:13:39,350 --> 00:13:42,280
checking to see if they put chocolates on my pillow yet.
一直來檢查我枕頭上 是不是有放巧克力

199
00:13:46,550 --> 00:13:48,610
- Hey, guys. - The chocolates aren't here.
-你們好 -巧克力還沒送來

200
00:13:48,790 --> 00:13:50,720
Damn it!
該死的！

201
00:13:50,890 --> 00:13:53,190
Ross just read me his speech. It's fantastic.
羅斯剛念了他的演講稿給我聽 真是精彩

202
00:13:53,390 --> 00:13:56,690
Oh, is it on the computer? Because I'd love to give it a read.
在電腦裡面嗎？因為我也想讀讀看

203
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:59,830
If you want to check your e-mail, just ask.
如果你想要查電子郵件就說吧

204
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,160
What? May I?
什麼？我可以嗎？

205
00:14:04,870 --> 00:14:09,810
What's with the rain, Geller? I mean, when I signed up for dino week..
那個雨是怎麼回事呢？蓋勒 我是說當我報名恐龍營的時候…

206
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:12,880
nobody said anything about it being monsoon season.
沒有人說過現在是雨季

207
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:16,680
- The wet season is June to December. - It's not the time, Charlie.
-雨季是六月到十二月 -現在不是時候，查莉

208
00:14:18,490 --> 00:14:20,420
Oh, no. No, no! Dear God, no!
哎呀，糟糕！親愛的上帝，不！

209
00:14:20,590 --> 00:14:23,820
What, did someone outbid you for the teapot?
怎麼了？有人搶先你標下茶壺嗎？

210
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:29,030
Secret teapot.
秘密茶壺

211
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:32,660
Your computer. I don't know what.. Everything's gone.
你的電腦，我不知道怎麼… 一切都不見了

212
00:14:32,870 --> 00:14:34,930
- What do you mean? - Must be a virus.
-你是什麼意思呢？ -一定是病毒

213
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:37,070
I think it erased your hard drive.
我想它把你的硬碟全殺掉了

214
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:39,570
What? Oh, my God. What did you do?
什麼？我的天啊！ 你幹了什麼好事？

215
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:42,110
Someone I don't know sent me an e-mail and I opened it.
一個我不認識的人寄了封信給我 然後我打開了它

216
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:46,040
- Why? Why would you open it? - Well, it didn't say, "This is a virus."
-為什麼？為什麼你要打開？ -那上面又沒有寫「這是病毒」

217
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:50,050
- What did it say? - "Nude.."
-那上面寫什麼？ -「裸體的…」

218
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:54,690
"Pictures of Anna Kournikova."
「安娜庫妮可娃的照片」

219
00:14:55,890 --> 00:14:58,290
- I'm so sorry. - What am I gonna do?
-我很抱歉 -我該怎麼辦呢？

220
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:00,550
- My speech is gone! - It's not gone.
-我的講稿不見了！ -沒有不見

221
00:15:00,730 --> 00:15:03,290
I'm sure you printed out a copy. You have a hard copy?
我相信你有列印出來，你有印出來嗎？

222
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:05,230
No, I don't!
不，我沒有！

223
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:09,940
Well, you must be pretty mad at yourself right now.
那你現在一定很氣自己

224
00:15:20,450 --> 00:15:22,780
- It's really gone? - Yep.
-真的不見了嗎？ -是的

225
00:15:22,950 --> 00:15:25,890
I'd like to thank you guys for coming down here..
我想要謝謝你們過來這裡…

226
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:28,890
to complain about the rain and ruin my career.
抱怨這些雨 然後毀了我的事業前途

227
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:30,960
- I just feel awful. - Yeah, you should.
-我覺得糟透了 -你的確應該

228
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:36,290
Nude pictures of Anna Kournikova? She's never even won a major tournament.
安娜庫妮可娃的裸照？ 她根本連什麼大獎都沒贏過

229
00:15:37,670 --> 00:15:40,400
Well, I tried Billie Jean King, but..
我是有試過比莉珍金，但是…

230
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:45,800
You know, you and Monica have the same I'm-gonna-kill-you look.
你知道嗎？你跟摩妮卡一樣都有那種 我想要殺死你的表情

231
00:15:45,970 --> 00:15:49,200
I can usually make it go away by kissing her.
我通常可以親她一下 就逃過一劫

232
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:52,040
Get out.
滾出去

233
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,980
You know, this happens all the time to my computer at work.
我工作的電腦也常常發生這種事

234
00:15:56,220 --> 00:15:57,980
- What do you do? - I usually go..
-那你怎麼辦呢？ -我通常會…

235
00:15:58,150 --> 00:16:00,380
play Tetris on somebody else's computer.
到別人的電腦上 玩俄羅斯方塊

236
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,220
I can't believe this is happening.
我不敢相信發生這種事

237
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,950
I have to give the keynote speech tomorrow.
我明天就要演講了

238
00:16:06,130 --> 00:16:09,860
I have to stand up in front of all these people. What am I gonna say?
我要站在所有人面前，我要說什麼呢？

239
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:13,160
You can use a speech I memorized for auditions.
你可以用我背下來 參加試演的那段話

240
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:17,130
I don't think your monologue from Star Wars is gonna help me right now.
我不認為你在《星際大戰》裡的獨白 可以對我有所幫助

241
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:20,470
Ross, we can solve this. I just heard your speech.
羅斯，不會有問題的 我聽過你的演講

242
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:25,440
- We can re-create it. We've got all night. - What, you really think we can do that?
-我們可以重建它，我們有一整晚 -什麼？你真的認為我們辦得到嗎？

243
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:28,880
Oh, wait. Joey and I are supposed to have dinner.
等等，喬伊跟我應該要共進晚餐的

244
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:31,480
Don't worry about that. I mean, Ross needs you.
別擔心，我知道羅斯需要你

245
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:35,450
Rachel and I will stay and help any way we can.
瑞秋跟我會留下來盡量幫忙

246
00:16:37,090 --> 00:16:39,790
All right. Okay, let's do it.
好的，我們來開始吧

247
00:16:40,190 --> 00:16:44,600
Well, I know we start by discussing the shortcomings of carbon dating.
我知道我們一開始 是討論碳年代測定法的缺點

248
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:48,330
And then I move on to what is clearly the defining moment..
然後我接著解說很明顯地什麼是…

249
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:53,060
of the Mesozoic Era, the breakup of Pangaea. Hello?
中生代的決定時刻，原始大陸的分裂 不是嗎？

250
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:57,400
And then there's the overview of the Triassic.
然後接下來是三疊紀的概觀

251
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:01,610
Any chance any of this happened in a galaxy far, far away?
有可能這一切都是在 很遠的銀河發生的嗎？

252
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,650
- Hello? - Okay, Mike?
-哈囉？ -好了，麥克？

253
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:14,450
Enough is enough. You love Phoebe, and she loves you.
鬧夠了，你愛菲比，而她也愛你

254
00:17:14,630 --> 00:17:17,220
So get over your I-never-wanna-get-married thing..
所以不要再說什麼 不想要結婚的話了

255
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,800
and step up!
趕快站出來！

256
00:17:19,370 --> 00:17:20,890
Who is this?
你是誰？

257
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,330
This is Monica, Phoebe's friend.
我是摩妮卡，菲比的朋友

258
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:27,370
Sure, Monica. So good to have you back in my life.
摩妮卡，你又回到我生命中 真是太好了

259
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:30,370
Listen, Phoebe is back with David.
聽著，菲比跟大衛復合了

260
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,710
He's gonna propose, and she's gonna say yes..
他即將要求婚，而她將會答應

261
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:35,180
but I know she really wants to be with you.
但是我知道 她真正想要的是跟你在一起

262
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:39,350
He's gonna propose?
他要求婚了？

263
00:17:39,990 --> 00:17:44,980
I'm sorry, did you say something? I can't hear through all this damned hair!
很抱歉，你說什麼呢？ 該死的頭髮遮住我聽不到！

264
00:17:46,030 --> 00:17:48,360
If Phoebe wants to marry David, she should.
如果菲比想要嫁給大衛，那就去吧

265
00:17:48,530 --> 00:17:51,430
I'm not gonna stand in the way of that. Neither should you.
我不會從中作梗，你也不應該

266
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:54,360
You don't tell me what to do. I tell you what to do.
你不用告訴我該怎麼做 我來告訴你怎麼做

267
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:58,690
Just call her. She's at the Paradise Hotel in Barbados.
打電話給她，她在巴貝多的天堂飯店

268
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:01,100
And while I've got you, you've got curly hair.
對了，你也有卷髮

269
00:18:01,310 --> 00:18:03,210
What do you do in the humidity?
在濕氣重的地方你怎麼辦呢？

270
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:07,210
Damn it!
該死的！

271
00:18:09,350 --> 00:18:13,450
- Well, I hope you're happy. - I hope you're happy too, honey.
-嗯，我希望你很快樂 -我也希望你很快樂

272
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,280
Phoebe's going to say yes to David.
菲比會答應大衛的求婚

273
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:22,190
- That's what happens when you meddle. - Phoebe's gonna say yes? That's great.
-這就是你愛管閒事的結果 -菲比要答應？太棒了

274
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:24,830
No, it's not. She's still in love with Mike.
不，一點也不，她還愛著麥克

275
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,300
- There's no chance that will work? - No, I called.
-那不會有什麼結果的嗎？ -沒有，我已經打過電話了

276
00:18:27,470 --> 00:18:30,900
- It's not gonna happen. - Meddler! Meddler!
-不會發生的 -雞婆！雞婆！

277
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:33,310
If you hadn't meddled to start with..
如果你不先多管閒事…

278
00:18:33,470 --> 00:18:36,140
then I wouldn't have had to go in and meddle myself.
那我就不用插手進來管事了

279
00:18:36,310 --> 00:18:39,400
No matter how much we meddle, we'll never be able to unmeddle..
不管我們插手多深 我們都沒有辦法補救…

280
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:42,450
the thing that you meddled up in the first place!
你一開始多管閒事惹出來的禍！

281
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:45,950
This vacation sucks!
這場假期真是爛！

282
00:18:47,926 --> 00:18:49,791
（歡迎古生物學家們）

283
00:18:51,790 --> 00:18:54,160
I'm so bored.
我好無聊

284
